Oracle fixtures

Frozen oracles: the pfb_unbound_*_oracle.json files

These files hold what the shipped pfb_unbound.py (CPython 3.11.15, maxminddb 3.2.0) decided, built and wrote for each scenario the Go tests replay (abp, build, control, gp, log_rows, observer, query, sqlite, stderr). The log-rows, observer and sqlite ones were recorded through the Python decider (dns_proxy/pfb_dns_proxy.py and dns_proxy/unbound_shim.py). Issue #3791 removed that decider and then pfb_unbound.py itself, so the generators (gen_pfb_unbound_<name>_oracle.py) can no longer run and were deleted; they stay in git history. The JSON files are frozen records: the Go tests in this directory compare against them and nothing regenerates them. To change a scenario, edit the JSON by hand, or check out the last commit that still has its generator (git log --diff-filter=D -- 'go/pfb_dns_gateway/decider/testdata/gen_pfb_unbound_<name>_oracle.py' names the removal; take its parent; the log-rows, observer and sqlite generators need a checkout from before the Python decider's removal), run the generator there as its header says, and copy the JSON back.

GeoLite2-Country-Test.mmdb and GeoIP2-Country-Test.mmdb are MaxMind's own test databases, test-data/ of https://github.com/maxmind/MaxMind-DB at commit 1b0113ab55f0428c00fe30b9709742ac52f4e9cc. That repository is dual-licensed Apache-2.0 / MIT (LICENSE-APACHE, LICENSE-MIT there), which this repository's Apache-2.0 licence accepts; they are used unmodified as test data only and are not shipped.
